{"request_id":"sha256:ce1295a4e4d9043dda08ebfd4df8756ab5ce37f32f976ae5e3c8c639864f999b","units":[{"unit_id":"sha256:885e215a010679cf5a16dd0d94e1a6bc49f846b7ac4702b9af3f735136afaf57","reviewed":true,"findings":[{"kind":"CAPACITY_QUALITATIVE","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":1022}],"reason":"Inventory accounting policy states that capitalization of indirect manufacturing costs is based on the normal utilization of the registrant's manufacturing facility in Texas, and that if manufacturing facility utilization is abnormally low, the portion of indirect manufacturing costs related to the abnormal utilization level is expensed as incurred. This is a qualitative statement about manufacturing capacity utilization at the Texas facility; no actual production quantity or available capacity figure is disclosed, so no utilization ratio can be computed."}],"unresolved":["The source states that indirect manufacturing cost capitalization depends on the normal utilization of the Texas manufacturing facility and that abnormally low utilization triggers expensing, but it does not disclose any actual production quantity, available capacity figure, or utilization percentage, so no production-to-capacity ratio can be derived from this disclosure."]}]}